ton below it.\\\\\\\" -p '5.2:' \\\\\\\"Guard earlier buttons after they are no longer last so pressing a non-last button does not append additional buttons.\\\\\\\" \\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$u\\\" section \\\"$PLAN_DIR\\\" step:01-define-button-chain-page/02-step-append-handler acceptance-criteria -p '\\\"'6.1:' \\\\\\\"After clicking the current last button before completion, the total button count increases by exactly one and the new button is visually below the previous last button.\\\\\\\" -p '6.2:' \\\\\\\"Clicking any button that is not currently last leaves the button count unchanged.\\\\\\\" \\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$u\\\" section \\\"$PLAN_DIR\\\" step:01-define-button-chain-page/02-step-append-handler handoff -p '\\\"'7.1:' \\\\\\\"W03 can rely on generated-button order and the current-last-button rule.\\\\\\\"\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$u\\\" section \\\"$PLAN_DIR\\\" step:01-define-button-chain-page/03-step-finish-handler instructions -p '\\\"'5.1:' \\\\\\\"In the future implementation, define finishOnFourthGeneratedButton() so the fourth generated button is the completion trigger.\\\\\\\" -p '5.2:' \\\\\\\"When that fourth generated button is clicked as the current last button, clear the document body and render only the completion state containing exact lowercase text finished.\\\\\\\" \\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$u\\\" section \\\"$PLAN_DIR\\\" step:01-define-button-chain-page/03-step-finish-handler acceptance-criteria -p '\\\"'6.1:' \\\\\\\"The completion click removes the button chain and no buttons remain visible.\\\\\\\" -p '6.2:' \\\\\\\"The completion text is exactly finished, all lowercase, with no extra visible words.\\\\\\\" \\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$u\\\" section \\\"$PLAN_DIR\\\" step:01-define-button-chain-page/03-step-finish-handler handoff -p '\\\"'7.1:' \\\\\\\"W04 can style the completion element produced by W03.\\\\\\\"\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"'$u\\\" section \\\"$PLAN_DIR\\\" step:01-define-button-chain-page/04-step-completion-border instructions -p '\\\"'5.1:' \\\\\\\"In the future implemen